# BMAD working output — tracked in full since 28 Aug 2026.
#
# It used to be that only the planning artifacts and the sprint tracker were
# kept, and everything under implementation-artifacts was treated as build
# scratch. That was right while this was a solo build: the specs were a record
# of work only one person would ever read.
#
# It stopped being right when the repository was handed to a teammate. The
# specs say why each story was built the way it was, deferred-work.md is the
# standing list of known problems and the reasoning behind each, and the epic
# contexts carry the constraints. Someone picking this up cold needs all of it,
# and 116 KB of markdown is a cheap price for not having to ask.
#
# `party-mode/` stays out: it is a scratch directory for an interactive
# brainstorming mode, not a record of anything the build depends on.
_bmad-output/party-mode/

# Claude Code worktrees — Lane B works in one; never commit a worktree tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# Story 5.4's approval-note tool writes real .docx files here at runtime
# (session cwd defaults to the repo root under `dsh --profile headless`).
# Generated output, never source.
/deliverables/
